<noinclude>
= Knowledge object =

Optional, explicit semantic metadata infobox for BITwiki public knowledge objects.

<pre>
{{Knowledge object
 |entity_type=Concept
 |domain=Biology, Philosophy
 |status=
 |provenance=
}}
</pre>

All four parameters may be omitted when the author cannot justify a value. Empty fields display ''Not specified'' without emitting semantic assertions. Do not invent a page-wide epistemic standing or provenance merely to complete an infobox. Consequential claims still require appropriate support and qualification in the article itself.

== Fields and semantics ==

* <code>entity_type</code> — primary type of the page's subject, when meaningful. The existing vocabulary is a reviewed baseline, not a limit on which subjects may be covered.
* <code>domain</code> — one or more subject fields separated by commas. <code>Module:Structure</code> emits distinct <code>Domain</code> Text-property annotations for each unique supplied value; this should be verified against the live semantic store before asserting production query behavior.
* <code>status</code> — optional epistemic standing. When supplied, it must be one of Hypothetical, Emerging, Supported, Well-supported, Established, or Disputed. The template deliberately does not store unsupported status labels.
* <code>provenance</code> — a concise source/origin or transformation note when useful. Ordinary article citations and page history are not replaced by this field.

Unregistered entity types or domains remain explicitly recorded as supplied and are flagged for review in [[:Category:BITwiki semantic vocabulary review]]. They are not silently remapped to a misleading existing type or used to deny a valid article. Maintainers should check for duplicates and justify vocabulary promotion rather than allowing unchecked synonym growth.

An invalid epistemic-status value produces a validation error in [[:Category:BITwiki semantic validation errors]]. Omitting a field is not an error.

== Implementation boundaries ==

<code>Template:Knowledge object</code> invokes <code>Module:Structure</code>, which delegates normalized field checks to <code>Module:BITwiki/Compiler</code> and reads the current controlled vocabulary from the source-controlled Lua schema projection.

The fields are a supplementary editorial and query surface, not a certificate of article accuracy or a universal schema for every discipline. The module does not prove cited claims, test all relationships, or establish that the target wiki has been deployed.

The <code>status</code> shown here is at most a page-level orientation. Contested interpretations, unknown mechanism, narrower evidence and contrary findings must be explained at claim or section level when consequential.

See [[BITwiki:Page format]], [[BITwiki:Entity types]], [[BITwiki:Semantic properties]], [[BITwiki:Epistemic status]], and [[BITwiki:Epistemics]].

